WTF: JSCOnly on Darwin uses time zone change notifications

Its CMake files build cocoa/TimeZoneCocoa.cpp on Darwin, which defines
listenForTimeZoneChangeNotifications(), but USE(TIME_ZONE_CHANGE_
NOTIFICATIONS) was off there, so TimeZone.cpp defined it as well and
the two clashed when JavaScriptCore was linked.

--- a/Source/WTF/wtf/PlatformUse.h	2026-11-07 01:38:18.146833697 -0500
+++ b/Source/WTF/wtf/PlatformUse.h	2026-11-07 01:38:41.580228845 -0500
@@ -70,7 +70,8 @@
 #define USE_GLIB 1
 #endif
 
-#if PLATFORM(COCOA) || USE(GLIB)
+/* JSCOnly on Darwin builds cocoa/TimeZoneCocoa.cpp too. */
+#if PLATFORM(COCOA) || USE(GLIB) || (defined(BUILDING_JSCONLY__) && OS(DARWIN))
 #define USE_TIME_ZONE_CHANGE_NOTIFICATIONS 1
 #endif
 
